    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Russell Estate Agents are delighted to present this attractive three-bedroom semi-detached home ideally situated in the popular residential development of Careystown Meadows, just a short stroll from the picturesque coastal village of Whitegate in East Cork. The property offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation arranged over two floors and is ideally suited to first-time buyers, young families or those looking to settle in a well-established residential area close to the coast. It is presented in excellent condition throughout with its current owners having completed a number of upgrades in the house in recent years. The property has the benefit of a B Ber rating ensure it qualifies for the green mortgage. Whitegate enjoys an attractive position on the eastern side of Cork Harbour and offers a good range of local amenities and recreational facilities, while Midleton is approximately 1215 minutes away by car. The wider area is particularly popular for its coastal setting, beaches, walks and sporting amenities. \n\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nEntrance Hallway \n\nKitchen / Dining room 5.95 m x 3.50m \n\nLiving room 4.17 m x 4.06 m\n\nGuest W.C. 1.52 m x 0.74 m\n\nFirst floor landing \n\nMaster Bedroom 3.85 m x 2.85 m\n\nEnsuite 2.56 m x 0.92 m\n\nBedroom 2 3.71 m x 3.17 m\n\nBedroom 3 2.64 m x 2.05 m & 1.08 m x 0.72 m\n\nBathroom 1.95 m x 1.67 m\n\n\nOUTSIDE\n\nThe property benefits from a well-proportioned rear garden, offering an attractive and practical outdoor space. A patio area provides an ideal setting for outdoor dining, entertaining or relaxing during the warmer months, while the adjoining lawn area offers plenty of space for children, pets or gardening enthusiasts. The garden also includes a useful garden shed, providing convenient storage for gardening equipment, bicycles and other outdoor items. Overall, the garden offers a pleasant combination of patio, lawn and practical storage, making it an excellent extension of the home.\n\nLOCATION\n\nWhitegate is a picturesque coastal village in East Cork, beautifully positioned on the eastern shores of Cork Harbour. Combining a rich maritime heritage with a strong sense of community, the village enjoys stunning waterfront views and a peaceful atmosphere, making it an attractive place to live and visit. \n\nSurrounded by scenic countryside and coastline, Whitegate offers easy access to nearby beaches, woodland walks, sailing facilities, and the renowned Trabolgan Holiday Village. The village is also within a short drive of Midleton, providing convenient access to an excellent range of shops, schools, restaurants, and commuter links to Cork City. \n\nWhitegate has a Eurospar supermarket selection of pubs and the well regarded Corkbeg Coffee on the seafront. It has a National School and there is a bus service to all of the Secondary Schools in Midleton also.\n\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\nFrom Midleton travel the R630 road to Whitegate. Continue ahead for 12 km and you will enter Whitegate village. Turn left as you enter the village and keep to the left. Continue ahead and Careystown Estate will be on your left hand side. Turn left into the estate and take the first left and left again and the house is ahead on the right hand side.\n\n\nVIEWING ARRANGEMENTS\n\nAll viewings of this property must be arranged through the selling agents Russell Estate Agents Limited. Our office hours are Monday to Friday 9am to 5pm. We can arrange evening and weekend viewings by prior appointment.\n\nNOTICE\n\nRussell Estate Agents for the vendors or lessors of this property whose agents they are, give notice that: (i) The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not institute, nor constitute part of, an offer or contract. (ii) All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for use and occupation, and any other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers or tenants should not rely on them as statements or representatives of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. (iii) No person in employment of Russell Estate Agents Limited has any authority to make or give representation or warranty in relation to this property. (iv) Prices are quoted exclusive of vat (unless otherwise stated) and all negotiations are conducted on the basis that the purchaser/lessee shall be liable for any VAT arising on the transaction. All maps are reproduced by Permission of the Ordnance Survey, License No. AU0066915 © Ordnance Survey Ireland / Government of Ireland."
      },
